-- *Five-day hysteresis after a service breakdown.* On day 2 of a five-day horizon, metro line A fails at 17:00 and imposes a 45-minute delay; the network is nominal again from day 3. <!-- source: experiments.yaml, exp_04a perturbation --> Three arms are compared: an agent with a short-term memory buffer in the sense of Park et al. (2023), decaying at rate λ; the same agent without memory; the tabular oracle, structurally memoryless. No survey follows the same travellers through such an event, so no value is a target. What is testable is the order of the arms on day 3, **[xx.y | exp_04a vs exp_04b vs exp_04c]**, the monotonic recovery over days 3 to 5, and the displacement of the curve when λ is divided by three, **[xx.y | exp_04d]**. The hypothesis falls if the memoryless agent shows the same inertia, if λ has no effect, or if recovery is not monotonic.
+- *Five-day hysteresis after a service breakdown.* On day 2 of a five-day horizon, metro line A fails at 17:00 and imposes a 45-minute delay; the network is nominal again from day 3. <!-- source: experiments.yaml, exp_04a perturbation --> Three conditions are compared: an agent with a short-term memory buffer in the sense of Park et al. (2023), decaying at rate λ; the same agent without memory; the tabular oracle, structurally memoryless. No survey follows the same travellers through such an event, so no value is a target. What is testable is the order of the conditions on day 3, **[xx.y | exp_04a vs exp_04b vs exp_04c]**, the monotonic recovery over days 3 to 5, and the displacement of the curve when λ is divided by three, **[xx.y | exp_04d]**. The hypothesis falls if the memoryless agent shows the same inertia, if λ has no effect, or if recovery is not monotonic.
 - *Five real, dated local news events.* From a corpus of 30 articles of the Toulouse press, an a priori grid written by the authors and frozen by git hash before any model call retains five events. <!-- source: RAPPORT_SCENARIOS_QUALITATIFS_TOULOUSE.md §2 and §3 --> Each acts through a distinct channel, and none is representable as a tabular variable: gusts of the Autan wind above 80 km/h closing the city's parks, a weather and physical-safety channel at metropolitan scale; a bed-bug scare in the metro and buses, a perceived-risk channel at network scale; an open-ended strike of waste collectors in the historic centre, a sensory-nuisance channel at district scale; the street parade of La Machine with a pedestrianised centre, a closure-and-attraction channel on the centre and its radial axes; the launch of electric bike-sharing on the hilly districts, a supply channel at metropolitan scale. Articles the grid discarded provide the placebo condition. Each event is run under five conditions on the same personas: nominal, raw article, mode-neutral paraphrase that removes every mention of a mode, placebo article, and the tabular oracle with the event encoded into its variables where the event admits such an encoding. The grid yields 4 × 5 = 20 signed directional predictions; we report the sign-agreement rate **[xx.y | exp_05]** and a weighted κ on predicted intensity, with option order randomised for every request as SILICA recommends (Bin Tareaf, 2026). The raw-minus-paraphrase contrast isolates instruction following from reasoning; the placebo contrast isolates specificity.
