-Section 2 defines the macro and micro metrics, the four rules of the contract, and the demographic control of the sealed cohort. Section 3 evaluates the bare LLMs and their inter-seed variability. Section 4 presents the four-level ablation, the calibrated and few-shot arms, the tabular references on the sealed survey test set, and the paired analysis of prompt enrichment against physical impedance, testing H0 and H1. Section 5 presents the two non-tabulated regimes, hysteresis and news events, under the pre-registered grid. Section 6 discusses the limits, including the independence-of-irrelevant-alternatives assumption of the renormalisation and the exposure asymmetry between oracle and agents, and the implications for hybrid designs. Section 7 concludes.
